.a is for archive

take all the files .c and change the extension

SRC = file.c
OBJS = $(SRC:.c=.o)
	OBJS variable declaration
	$(SRCSi...) content SRCS access
	:.c=:.o substitute suffix .c with .o
-> to remember 
	$(VAR:old=new)
this line does not compile anything, it creates a list of names. If SRCS has ft_printf.c the variable OBJS has simply the word ft+printf.o

once I have the list of the objs I can give the rule to create the library 

Rules	|
--------|

target: prerequisites
	command
target is what I want to creare: all, clean, the name of the libftprintf.a
prerequisites: dependencies, the files or the necessary rules to build the target.
command: the action to do, preceded by TAB

all is the unique rule doesn't do anything byt to call the prncipal target
all : $(NAME)
---	----
|	-> real target must be created
|->formal target

so when I do
	make
then it search
	all
and "all" says "to finish I need exists $(NAME)

$(NAME):  OBJS(OBJS)
	ar rcs $(NAME) $(OBJS)	
$(NAME) says "to be build I need all the files $(OBJS)"
when the objects are ready it executes the command ar rcs
ar creates an archive:many little packages are created .o and are packaged into a file .zip or .tar optimized to the compiler.
what does ar rcs libftprintf.a *.c does ?
r - replace or if .o it is already inside it is updated
c - create the library if it does not exist
s - sort create an index of symbols inside thant helps the compiler to find quickly the file .c inside the archive, example ft_printf.c

IMPLICIT RULE
%.o:%.c
	...
	$<c means the source file
	$@ means the file target

clean : NO PREREQUISITES 
	rm -f OBJECTS
fclean : clean
	-------
	ensure that clean has been done then fclean
	rm -rf libftprintf.a

RELINK
re : fclean name
	    ----
	    target all
     -------
     first execute target fclean then target all
.PHONY
it is useful to discoupling the name of a rule from the existence of a real file


========BUILDING===========================================
ft_printf must take many arguments "..."

	<type> ft_printf(<argument>, ...)

where I can put all these extra arguments ?
a box is needed
	va_list args (variadic arguments list)
	HOW TO THINK
	where do I put all these extra arguments? 
	-> declaration and creation of the box
		va_list args; (variadic arguments list)

opening the stock (box)
	the stock is closed it must be opened and establish from were to start counting
	-> open the stock after the last known parameter "format"
		va_start(args, format);

loop: a while to run in the string character by character


close the stock
	-> va_end(args);

in the end how many pieces gave
	lenght

==================================
DETAILS
a loop while where:
format == '%' arrive until you see %
format[i+1] if at i I had '%' then i+1 is the 'letter after %'
	-> ft_printf("hello world %d", 42);
	format[i] at '%'
	then format[i] ad 'd'

a funcion ft_format will print the number or the string and return the number of bytes printed.
that number must be added to the length counter.

ft_putchar_fd_len: prints a char and returns the  1
